--
--  Functional Coverage /
--  Test Description:
--
--  * Ensures that a frame will not be copied to memory if the GEM is transmitting 
--     in half 
--    duplex mode at the time a destination address is received.
--  * Ensures that the GEM does proper external address recognition.
--  * Ensures that the GEM does proper address recognition for broadcast 
--    addressing in 1000 mode.
--  * Ensures that the GEM does proper address recognition for unicast hash 
--    addressing in 1000 mode.
--  * Ensures that the GEM does proper address recognition for multicast hash 
--    addressing in 1000 mode.
--  * Ensure that the all of the specific address registers work properly.
--
--  Detailed Test Description
--  1. Initialise GEM for 1000-mode operation and external address match enable.
--  2. Check status registers to ensure they have the proper value after reset.
--  3. Write an address to specific address register one.
--  4. Transmit a frame with extension.
--  5. Start receiving a frame with extension.  (The GEM should not be able to receive a 
--     frame because the GEM is currently transmitting a frame)
--  6. Check the interrupt status register once the frame is completely transmitted.
--  7. Receive a frame with extension that matches both the external address and local 
--     address. (Local addresses are in the specific address registers)
--  8. Check the interrupt status register once the frame is completely received.
--
--  External Addressing:
--  9. Write new addresses to all the local address registers so that there is no local 
--     address match. Therefore, the next received frame will only match on external address.
--  10. Receive a frame with extension that will only match on external address. The frame 
--      should be accepted and written to memory.
--  11. Check the interrupt status register once the frame is completely received.
--  12. Disable external address matching and receive a broadcast frame. The frame should 
--      be written to memory.  (The broadcast address of 0xffffffffffff is recognised if 
--      the 'no broadcast' bit in the network configuration register is zero)
--  13. Check the interrupt status register once the frame is completely received.
--  14. Repeat external address matching for each of the external address match pins.
--
--  Copy all frames:
--  15. Enable the GEM to copy all frames and send a broadcast frame with extension. 
--      (This frame should be copied to memory but should not set any of the address 
--      matching status bits)
--  16. Check the interrupt status register and the receive status register 
--      once the frame is completely received.
--
--  Unicast Hash Addressing:
--  17. Initialise the GEM for unicast hash addressing.
--  18. Set the hash register bottom to 0 hex and only set bit 57 in the 
--      hash register top.
--  19. Receive a frame with extension with the destination address set to 
--      "1111aaaaaaaa".  The hashing of this destination address reduces to '111001' (57 decimal) 
--      or bit 57 in the hash address registers. (This frame should be stored to memory)
--  20. Check the interrupt status register once the frame is completely received.
--  21. Now set all hash indices (set all the bits in the hash registers) except bit 57.
--  22. Receive the same frame with the same destination address as in point 18. 
--      (This frame should be discarded.)
--  23. Receive a broadcast frame with extension. (The multicast frame bit is not enabled. 
--      Therefore, this frame should be discarded because it's a type of multicast frame.)
--  24. Set hash register bit 10 and clear all the remaining bits. (hash index of 10 decimal)
--  25. Receive a frame with extension with the destination address set to 'aaaa22222222'. 
--      The hashing of this destination address reduces to '001010' (10 decimal) or bit 10 
--      in the hash address registers. (This frame should be stored to memory)
--  26. Check the interrupt status register once the frame is completely received.
--  27.  Set hash register bit 27 and clear all the remaining bits. (hash index of 27 decimal)
--  28. Receive a frame with extension with the destination address set to '1111aaaaaaaa'. 
--      The hashing of this destination address reduces to '011011' (27 decimal) or bit 27 
--      in the hash address registers. (This frame should be stored to memory)
--  29. Check the interrupt status register once the frame is completely received.
--
--  Multicast Hash Addressing:
--  30. Initialise the GEM for multicast hash addressing.
--  31. Set hash register bit 5 and clear all the remaining bits. (hash index of 5 decimal)
--  32. Receive a frame with extension with the destination address set to 'ffffbbbbbbbb'.  
--      The hashing of this destination address reduces to '000101' (5 decimal) or bit 5 in 
--      the hash address registers. (This frame should be stored to memory)
--  33. Check the interrupt status register once the frame is completely received.
--  34. Now set all hash indices (set all the bits in the hash registers) except bit 5.
--  35. Receive the same frame with the same destination address as in point 31. 
--      (This frame should be discarded.)
--  36. Receive a frame with extension with the destination address set to 'ffff77777777'. 
--      The hashing of this destination address reduces to '001010' (10 decimal) or bit 10 
--      in the hash address registers. (This frame should be stored to memory since all 
--      hash indices are enabled except 5)
--  37. Check the interrupt status register once the frame is completely received.
--
--  Specific Address Register Two:
--  38. Clear the hash registers.
--  39. Enable the GEM for all address matching (unicast, and multicast) except 
--      for copy all frames.
--  40. Write an address to specific address register two.
--  41. Receive a frame with extension.
--  42. Receive a frame with extension that matches the local address. 
--      (Local addresses are in the specific address registers)
--  43. Check the interrupt status register once the frame is completely received.
--
--  Specific Address Register Three:
--  44. Write an address to specific address register three.
--  45. Receive a frame with extension.
--  46. Receive a frame with extension that matches the local address. 
--      (Local addresses are in the specific address registers)
--  47. Check the interrupt status register once the frame is completely received.
--
--  Specific Address Register Four:
--  48. Write an address to specific address register four.
--  49. Receive a frame with extension.
--  50. Receive a frame with extension that matches the local address. 
--      (Local addresses are in the specific address registers)
--  51. Check the interrupt status register once the frame is completely received.
--
--  Specific Address Register Three:
--  52. Write an address to specific address register three.
--  53. Receive a frame with extension.
--  54. Receive a frame with extension that matches the local address. 
--      (Local addresses are in the specific address registers)
--  55. Check the interrupt status register once the frame with extension is 
--      completely received. Check all status and statistic registers and 
--      ensure that the above operations were dealt with properly.
--  56. Receive a frame with extension and ensure that external address 
--      match happens too late.
--  57. Receive a frame with extension and have an external match as a 
--      strobe during the external match acceptance window.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
